{
  "_comment": "Count ratchets (A8, small form), enforced by scripts/test_count_ratchets.py on every push. Two hard checks: the number of *columns.test.js contract files per lambda directory, and which scripts/layout-gate scripts may drive Chrome without the exit watchdog. Both are debt counters that may FALL, never RISE without a recorded reason.",
  "_why": "Contract files were growing by about one a day, each a new vitest file paying its own jsdom start-up, because every remedy text in the repo said 'always a new file'. The schema audit reads one keyed AUDIT_COLUMNS object per file and 30 files already declare several relations in it, so a new JOIN belongs as a key in a file the directory already has. Separately, the exit watchdog only protects a gate that imports it; ten Chrome-driving scripts never did, and a new one could join them unnoticed.",
  "_measured_at": "origin/dev daf8042bd50d923c41d68fb60f771ad59f3eeb26",
  "_how_to_raise": "Only a columns ceiling can be raised, and only when the directory has no keyed contract file of its own or the new contract cannot share one. In ONE commit: (1) raise that directory's number in columns_tests_per_dir (a directory not listed has ceiling 0: add it); (2) add the new file name to columns_test_files for that directory; (3) append a row to raises: {\"what\": \"lambda/<dir>\", \"from\": <old ceiling>, \"to\": <new ceiling>, \"why\": \"<why an existing keyed file could not take the contract>\", \"work_item\": \"<ID>\"}. Leave _start alone: it is the history the rows are checked against. No approval is needed; the row is the review surface (git log -p scripts/count-ratchets.json). watchdog_exempt cannot be raised: a new gate imports armExitWatchdog.",
  "_how_to_lower": "No row needed. When a columns file is deleted or folded into a sibling, lower that directory's number and remove the name from columns_test_files. When an exempt gate script gains the watchdog or is deleted, remove its name from watchdog_exempt. The test reds until you do, so headroom never accumulates.",
